          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            Full de Sitter spacetime is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lorentzian+manifold"} Lorentzian manifold
            which is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coset+space"} coset space
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lorentz+groups"} Lorentz groups
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi dS
                    %mi d
                  %mo ≃
                  %mi O
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi d
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi O
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi d
                  %mo −
                  %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  dS^d \simeq O(d,1)/O(d-1,1)
          %p
            This models a cosmology
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/FRW+model"} FRW model
            for positive
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cosmological+constant"} cosmological constant
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dark+energy"} dark energy
          %p
            Similarly
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/anti+de+Sitter+spacetime"} anti de Sitter spacetime
            is
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi adS
                    %mi d
                  %mo ≃
                  %mi O
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi d
                  %mo −
                  %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi O
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi d
                  %mo −
                  %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  adS^d \simeq O(d-1,2)/O(d-1,1)
          %p
            (e.g.
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#Blau"} Blau §39.1
          %p This admits different spatial slicings of relevance:
          %p
            %img{:src => "https://ncatlab.org/nlab/files/deSitterSlicings.png", :width => "600"}/
          %blockquote
            %p
              graphics grabbed from
              %a{:href => "https://physics.stackexchange.com/a/353157/5603"} this Physics.SE comment
