          %h2#References References
          %h3#in_classical_gravity In classical gravity
          %ul
            %li#CastellaniDAuriaFre
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Leonardo+Castellani"}> Leonardo Castellani
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Riccardo+D%27Auria"} Riccardo D'Auria
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pietro+Fr%C3%A9"} Pietro Fré
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Supergravity+and+Superstrings+-+A+Geometric+Perspective"} Supergravity and Superstrings - A Geometric Perspective
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1142/0224"} doi:10.1142/0224
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/CastellaniDAuriaFre-ChI3.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/CastellaniDAuriaFre-ChI4.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
            %li#Blau
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Matthias+Blau"}> Matthias Blau
                , §39 of:
                %em Lecture notes on general relativity
                (
                %a{:href => "http://www.blau.itp.unibe.ch/GRLecturenotes.html"}> web
                )
            %li
              %p
                Thomas Hartman,
                %em Lecture Notes on Classical de Sitter Space
                (
                %a{:href => "http://www.hartmanhep.net/GR2017/desitter-lectures-v2.pdf"}> pdf
                ,
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/HartmanDeSitterSpacetime.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
            %li
              %p
                Marcus Spradlin,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andrew+Strominger"} Andrew Strominger
                %em Les Houches Lectures on De Sitter Space
                (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0110007"}> arXiv:hep-th/0110007
                )
          %p See also:
          %ul
            %li
              Wikipedia,
              %em
                %a{:href => "http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/De_Sitter_space"} de Sitter space
          %p
            With focus on methods of
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/conformal+geometry"} conformal geometry
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Juan+A.+Valiente+Kroon"}> Juan A. Valiente Kroon
              , chapter 15 of:
              = succeed "," do
                %em Conformal Methods in General Relativity
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1017/9781009291309"} doi:10.1017/9781009291309
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://library.oapen.org/handle/20.500.12657/59217"} oapen:20.500.12657/59217
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://library.oapen.org/bitstream/id/548cfabe-a25b-4562-b95e-aa2894525f32/9781009291309.pdf"} pdf
          %p
            Further discussion of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/de+Sitter+group"} de Sitter group
            and its
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representation+theory"} representation theory
          %ul
            %li
              Vladimir Schaub,
              %em
                A Walk Through
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Spin
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %mi d
                      %mo +
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Spin(1,d+1)
              \&amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2405.01659"}> arXiv:2405.01659
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %h3#InPerturbativeQuantumGravity In perturbative quantum gravity
          %p
            Discussion of de Sitter spacetime in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/perturbative+quantum+gravity"} perturbative quantum gravity
            and its infrared instability, includes the following:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Emil+Mottola"}> Emil Mottola
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Particle creation in de Sitter space
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevD.31.754"} doi:10.1103/PhysRevD.31.754
            %li#Witten01
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Edward+Witten"}> Edward Witten
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Quantum Gravity In De Sitter Space
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "http://theory.tifr.res.in/strings/"} Strings 2001
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0106109"} arXiv:hep-th/0106109
            %li
              %p
                Dietmar Klemm, Luciano Vanzo,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Aspects of Quantum Gravity in de Sitter Spaces
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0407255"} arXiv:hep-th/0407255
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Richard+Woodard"}> Richard Woodard
                ,
                %em De Sitter Breaking in Field Theory
                (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/gr-qc/0408002"}> arXiv:gr-qc/0408002
